%H A400814 David Smith, Joseph Samuel Myers, Craig S. Kaplan, and Chaim Goodman-Strauss, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.17743">A chiral aperiodic monotile</a>, arXiv:2305.17743 [math.CO], 2023-2024.
%H A400814 <a href="/index/Rec#order_05">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (13,-44,28,5,-1).
%F A400814 Conjecture: a(n) = 13*a(n-1) - 44*a(n-2) + 28*a(n-3) + 5*a(n-4) - a(n-5) for n >= 5.
%F A400814 Conjectured g.f.: 2*x^3*(5 + 3*x)/((1 - x)*(1 - 8*x + x^2)*(1 - 4*x - x^2)).
%F A400814 a(n) = (19*A057080(n-1) - A057080(n))/30 - A014445(n)/2 + 2/3 for n >= 1.
%F A400814 Limit_{n->oo} a(n)/A057080(n) = (75-19*sqrt(15))/30 = 0.0471105474... (one minor star triple for every (75+19*sqrt(15))/7 = 21.2266690... tiles).
%F A400814 Limit_{n->oo} (A400813(n) - a(n))/A400812(n) = 1/sqrt(15) = 0.2581988897... (the asymptotic excess of major over minor star triples is 1/sqrt(15), about 25.82%, of all star triples).
%e A400814 a(3) = 10: the level-3 supertile (559 tiles) contains 28 star triples, 18 major and 10 minor (5 in each of two orientations).
%Y A400814 Cf. A400812 (all star triples), A400813 (major star triples), A057080 (all tiles).
%Y A400814 Minor star triples are central in Type C megastars (A400810) and first in clusters of family A (A397115).
